	"AlternateLoadingTips": {
		"1": "Advanced players may wish to remap their buttons; you can do this in Settings.",
		"2": "The Housing menu allows you to decide what rooms you want your NPCs to live in.",
		"3": "Press {InputTriggerUI_ZoomIn} and {InputTriggerUI_ZoomOut} to zoom in & out! Focus on what matters!"
	},
	"Tutorial": {
		"IntroMessage": "Welcome to Terraria! To start the tutorial, come talk to me! You can use [cm:0]to move, [cm:1]to Aim, and [cm:3]to Jump! To talk to me, use [cm:1]to aim near me and press [cm:4]for your first lesson!  Press [cb:1]to close this window.",
		"CopperAxe": "Hello! I'm Andrew your guide. To get started the most important thing we need is shelter. To get Wood [i:9]we need to chop down a tree.\n\nTake this Copper Axe [i:3506]. Use [cm:9]/[cm:10]to select the Copper Axe in your hotbar. Then press [cm:2]to chop down a tree and bring back 10 Wood.",
		"NeedMoreWood": "We need 10 Wood [i:9]. With a Copper Axe [i:3506] selected in your hotbar, press [cm:2]to chop down a tree and bring back 10 Wood.",
		"HaveWood": "Now we need to craft this Wood into a Work Bench [i:36]. Press [cm:5]to open your Inventory and [cm:7][cm:8]to navigate to your crafting list panel. From the crafting list, highlight the Work Bench [i:36]and press [cm:12]to craft it. When you have crafted a Work Bench, come talk to me.",
		"WorkBenchCrafted": "Oh, I guess you don't need to learn about crafting then!",
		"WorkBenchPlace": "This Work Bench [i:36]needs to be placed on the ground. Use [cm:9][cm:10]to highlight the Work Bench in your hotbar. Then use [cm:1] to aim at a place on the ground and press [cm:2]to place it.",
		"WorkBenchAlreadyPlaced": "You've got the hang of placing items.",
		"CraftChairDoor": "Excellent. Now we need a house to live in. I started this one here, but to be a valid house it needs a chair, a table or work bench, and a door. You can make these from the Crafting panel by standing near a Work Bench.\n\nCraft a Wooden Chair [i:34], a Wooden Table [i:32]and a Wooden Door [i:25]and use [cm:2]to place them in the house for me. You may need to chop down more trees!",
		"CraftLightsKillSlimes": "This is looking better, now we need lights! To craft Torches [i:8]we need to combine Gel [i:23]and Wood [i:9]. Gel is dropped by Slimes when they are defeated.\n\nTake this Copper Shortsword [i:3507]and select it in the hotbar with [cm:9][cm:10]. Press [cm:2]to defeat a Slime and collect it's Gel.",
		"CraftLightsKillSlimes2": "To craft Torches [i:8]we need to combine Gel [i:23]and Wood [i:9]. Gel is dropped by Slimes when they are defeated. Select your [i:3507]Copper Shortsword in the hotbar with [cm:9][cm:10]. Press [cm:2]to defeat a Slime and collect it's Gel.",
		"CraftLightsCraftTorches": "If you take damage from an enemy, try eating a Mushroom [i:5]or you can find Healing Potions [i:28]in pots and chests hidden in the world.\nCraft the Gel [i:23]and Wood [i:9]to make Torches [i:8]and then use [cm:2]to place them on the walls to light up the house.",
		"CraftLightsValidHouse": "Great, now this place feels like home. Its time to do some digging. Take this Copper Pickaxe [i:3509]and dig up some Iron Ore [i:11]. There should be Iron Ore in the nearby caves. We need 15 Iron Ore [i:11]. \n\nRemember to carry some Torches [i:8]to light your way and if you get stuck, I also gave you Rope [i:965]to place to climb out!",
		"CollectOres": "Using your Copper Pickaxe [i:3509]dig up Iron Ore [i:11]. There should be some in the nearby caves. We need 15 Iron Ore [i:11].",
		"FurnaceSmelt": "While you were digging I made this Furnace [i:33], Find it in your Inventory and place it on the ground. Then craft the Iron Ore [i:11]into 5 Iron Bars [i:22]!",
		"FurnaceSmelt2": "Using your placed Furnace [i:33]craft the Iron Ore [i:11]into 5 Iron Bars [i:22]!",
		"Anvil": "Once you start smelting bars, you'll need an anvil to make even more items. Craft an Iron Anvil [i:35]at the Work Bench [i:36]and place it by your Furnace [i:33].",
		"CraftCopperArmour": "Now the world out there gets dangerous the further you get from home. You'll need some armor to help keep you safe when you're exploring. Here are enough Copper Bars [i:20]to make some shiny new armor.\n\nCraft a Copper Helmet [i:89], Copper Chainmail [i:80]and Copper Greaves [i:76]while standing near the Anvil [i:35].",
		"CraftCopperArmour2": "Craft a Copper Helmet [i:89], Copper Chainmail [i:80]and Copper Greaves [i:76]while standing near the Anvil [i:35].",
		"EquipArmour": "When you have an item which can be equipped from your inventory, press [cm:14]to equip it. Alternatively you can press [cm:13]to pick it up and navigate with [cm:7]/[cm:8]to the Equipment Menu and place it into the appropriate slot.",
		"KillZombies": "Now you look ready to take on a few more challenges. Its gotten dark out, and at night some terrible creatures come to bang at the door. If you feel brave you can take this Iron Bow [i:99]and these Wooden Arrows [i:40]and go and kill a few Zombies and Demon Eyes if you dare.",
		"OpenBestiary": "Keep an eye out for items dropped by enemies. You can find out which enemies drop what loot opening the Bestiary from either the [cm:5]Inventory or the [cm:15]Pause Menu. Open it to see all the People, Animals and Monsters you've met in the world!",
		"OpenSettings": "The [cm:15]Settings menu has an array of options to allow you to customize the game especially for your playstyle. If you find it hard to see the Inventory, you can Edit the Layout from the Interface tab and adjust nearly everything about the interface. You can also change all your button bindings in the Controller tab and Edit Controller Bindings.",
		"Complete": "This world is just a temporary place which resets when you Exit. Now go create your own unique Character and World to explore. Press [cm:15]and Exit to your own world!"
	},
	"TutorialTouch": {
		"IntroMessage": "Welcome to Terraria! To start the tutorial, come talk to me! You can use [ta:0] to move, [ta:1] to Aim, and [ct:6] to Jump! To talk to me, stand nearby and tap me for your first lesson!  Press [ct:8] to close this window.",
		"CopperAxe": "Hello! I'm Andrew your guide. To get started the most important thing we need is shelter. To get Wood [i:9]we need to chop down a tree.\n\nTake this Copper Axe [i:3506]. Tap to select the Copper Axe in your hotbar. Then press [ct:7,3506] to chop down a tree and bring back 10 Wood.",
		"NeedMoreWood": "We need 10 Wood [i:9]. With a Copper Axe [i:3506] selected in your hotbar, press [ct:7,3506] to chop down a tree and bring back 10 Wood.",
		"HaveWood": "Now we need to craft this Wood into a Work Bench [i:36]. Tap [ct:9] to open your Inventory and [ct:5] to open to your crafting list panel. From the crafting list, highlight the Work Bench [i:36] and tap to craft it. When you have crafted a Work Bench, come talk to me.",
		"WorkBenchPlace": "This Work Bench [i:36]needs to be placed on the ground. Tap to highlight the Work Bench in your hotbar. Then use [ta:1] to aim at a place on the ground and tap to place it. You can also press anywhere on the screen to start placing it too!",
		"CraftChairDoor": "Excellent. Now we need a house to live in. I started this one here, but to be a valid house it needs a chair, a table or work bench, and a door. You can make these from the Crafting panel by standing near a Work Bench.\n\nCraft a Wooden Chair [i:34], a Wooden Table [i:32]and a Wooden Door [i:25]and tap to place them in the house for me. You may need to chop down more trees!",
		"CraftLightsKillSlimes": "This is looking better, now we need lights! To craft Torches [i:8]we need to combine Gel [i:23]and Wood [i:9]. Gel is dropped by Slimes when they are defeated.\n\nTake this Copper Shortsword [i:3507]and select it in the hotbar by tapping it. Press [ct:7,3507] to defeat a Slime and collect it's Gel.",
		"CraftLightsKillSlimes2": "To craft Torches [i:8]we need to combine Gel [i:23]and Wood[i:9]. Gel is dropped by Slimes when they are defeated. Select your [i:3507]Copper Shortsword in the hotbar by tapping it.\nPress [ct:7,3507] to defeat a Slime and collect it's Gel.",
		"CraftLightsCraftTorches": "If you take damage from an enemy, try eating a Mushroom [i:5]or you can find Healing Potions [i:28]in pots and chests hidden in the world.\n\nCraft the Gel [i:23]and Wood [i:9]to make Torches [i:8]and then tap to place them on the walls to light up the house.",
		"EquipArmour": "When you have an item which can be equipped from your inventory, press [ct:11] to equip it. Alternatively you can press and hold to pick it up, drag it to the Equipment Menu and place it into the appropriate slot.",
		"OpenBestiary": "Keep an eye out for items dropped by enemies. You can find out which enemies drop what loot opening the Bestiary from either the [ct:9]Inventory or the [ct:10]Pause Menu. Open it to see all the People, Animals and Monsters you've met in the world!",
		"OpenSettings": "The [ct:10]Settings menu has an array of options to allow you to customize the game especially for your playstyle. If you find it hard to see the Inventory, you can Edit the Layout from the Interface tab and adjust nearly everything about the interface.",
		"Complete": "This world is just a temporary place which resets when you Exit. Now go create your own unique Character and World to explore. Press [ct:10]and Exit to your own world!"
	},
}
